{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Making a Difference"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Florence Nightingale"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 14}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe the reasons or results of events or actions in spoken or written texts, in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le14ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Past Perfect with Other Time Expressions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use different time expressions with the Past Perfect tense to refer to events that occurred before others in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Let's look at different examples to see how you can use the Past Perfect with various time expressions.<br/><br/>  <div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">as soon as<br/> immediately<br/> the moment</span></span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I drove to the hospital <span class=\"strong\">the moment I had gotten</span> the text message about the car accident.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">The moment I had gotten</span> the text message about the car accident, I drove to the hospital.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Which action happened first? <span class=\"strong\">As soon as/ immediately/ the moment</span> + past perfect tells you the first action in these sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">before</span></span><br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Before</span> I <span class=\"strong\">had decided</span> on a ring for my fianc\u00e9e, I looked at several pictures of rings with her mother and sisters.<br/> I looked at several pictures of rings with her mother and sisters <span class=\"strong\">before</span> I <span class=\"strong\">had decided</span> on a ring for my fianc\u00e9e.</span><br/><br/>   Which action happened first? <span class=\"strong\">Before</span> + past perfect tells you the second action in these sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">until/ till</span></span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I discussed several different vacation spots with my friends <span class=\"strong\">until/ till</span> we <span class=\"strong\">had chosen</span> where to go on holiday.</span><br/><br/>   What about in this sentence? <span class=\"strong\">Until/ till</span> + past perfect tells you that this action may come after the other action in the main clause."}, {"type": "example", "content": "As soon as she was ready, he had taught her languages, literature, history, and mathematics. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Until Florence had decided to become a nurse, her parents were happy with her decisions. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Result Clause: Such/So That"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can talk about the results of actions or situations by using structures with <span class=\"italic\">so that</span> and <span class=\"italic\">such</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to talk about the effect of something or the result, you can use: <span class=\"strong\"><ul><li>such + adjective + noun + that <li>so + adjective/ adverb + that</li></ul></span> <span class=\"italic\">Roberto was <span class=\"strong\">such</span> <span class=\"underline\">a handsome man</span> <span class=\"strong\">that</span> people often mistook him for a celebrity or a supermodel.</span><br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">Maria was <span class=\"strong\">so</span> <span class=\"underline\">tired</span> <span class=\"strong\">that</span> <span class=\"underline\">she went to bed without even changing into her pyjamas.</span><br/> <span class=\"underline\">The snow fell <span class=\"strong\">so</span></span> heavily <span class=\"strong\">that</span> it was impossible to see a few feet in front of you.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\"><ul><li>such + a + adjective + noun + that OR <li>so + adjective + a + noun + that</li></ul></span> You only use these structures with a singular noun that follows a/ an. Remember to change the order of the article a/an and the noun when you use <span class=\"strong\">so</span>.<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">It was <span class=\"strong\">such a </span><span class=\"underline\">windy day</span><span class=\"strong\"> that</span> thousands of homes were left without electricity when trees tore down overhead power lines.<br/><br/>  It was <span class=\"strong\">so</span><span class=\"underline\"> windy</span><span class=\"strong\"> a</span> <span class=\"underline\">day </span><span class=\"strong\">that </span>thousands of homes were left without electricity when trees tore down overhead power lines.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can also use <span class=\"strong\">so</span> at the beginning of your sentence. This is more for emphasis of the adjective and noun. If you use <span class=\"strong\">so </span>at the beginning of your sentence, the position of the verb changes.<br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\"> He was <span class=\"strong\">so</span> rich <span class=\"strong\">that</span> he could have bought a private jet for each member of his family.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">So</span> rich <span class=\"strong\">was he that </span>he could have bought a private jet for each member of his family.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "She got offers of marriage, but she was so persistent in wanting to be a nurse, that when she was 31, her father agreed to let her become one."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There were such unsanitary conditions in the military hospital that she was shocked. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "modern thinker"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "person who advocates or practices a departure from traditional styles or values "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Her father was such a modern thinker that decided that women Florence should have a good education."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le14ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about medical issues."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cholera"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an infectious and often fatal bacterial disease of the small intestine"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Soldiers also died of cholera and malaria. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le14ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "malaria"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "fever caused by a parasite that invades the red blood cells."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Soldiers also died of cholera and malaria. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le14ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "virulent "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "extremely severe or harmful in its effects"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Before she had cleaned and organized the hospital, it was conducive to the spread of virulent disease."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le14ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unappealing"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not inviting or attractive "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The food for patients was so unappealing that she had bought fruit, vegetables with her own money. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le14ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mortality rate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " the number of deaths in a given area or period, or from a particular cause"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Suddenly the mortality rate had plummeted from 60% to 2.2%. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le14ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rounds "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an act of visiting each of a number of people or places"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Florence was such a devoted nurse that she was often seen at night walking the halls carrying a lamp, doing her rounds."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le14ob07aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write down a few points that you would like to discuss about the medical system in your country - both positive and negative points. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Back up each point with an example say what had happened."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice stating your points and backup examples."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss your ideas with a partner or group."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write points about the medical system in my city and country."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I find evidence to support my points."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss my ideas and give feedback on other ideas."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"ty